+## Tested on hardware
+
+An Apple TV 4K (2nd generation) on tvOS 27.0 accepts the default-signed tag. Two 7.1.4
+programmes, a spoken height check and a heights-only demo, were encoded with `forge atmos-cbi` at
+768 kbps, each beside a DEE 5.2.1 encode of the same WAV, and played with AVPlayer into a Samsung
+HW-Q990C. tvOS's E-AC-3 JOC decoder was also run in process (`'ec+3'` through `AVAudioConverter`)
+to read each output channel's level.
+
+- **Signed:** tvOS reconstructs the objects. Each height channel's content came out of the
+  matching height output and nothing leaked into the surrounds. In a blind listen beside DEE's
+  encode, both played the heights-only demo overhead.
+- **One primary-tag bit flipped per frame**, with `crc2` re-stamped and nothing else changed:
+  tvOS outputs silence, in playback and in the in-process decode alike. It mutes the stream
+  rather than falling back to the bed.
+- **Level:** this encoder writes `joc_clipgain_x_bits` as 0, which this project's decoder reads as
+  unity but tvOS applies as exactly 1/16 (-24 dB) to the reconstructed objects. DEE writes 4; with
+  4, tvOS's object levels matched this project's own decode within 0.2 dB.
+
+Only this device and OS were tested; other certified decoders may gate differently.
+
